```
if ('Notification' in window) {
  Notification.requestPermission()
}
```

Once permission is granted, you can use the `Notification` interface to create and display notifications:

```
if (Notification.permission === 'granted') {
  new Notification('New game highlight! ', {
    body: 'Your favorite team just scored a goal!' })
}
```

To trigger these notifications, you can use `setInterval` to periodically check the scores and compare them to the previous scores. If there is a significant change, you can display a notification to the user. In addition to browser notifications, you can also send push notifications to mobile devices using a third-party service like Firebase Cloud Messaging. This requires additional setup and configuration, but it allows users to receive notifications even when they are not actively using the web application.
